      "text": "🇺🇸 TRUMP ADMINISTRATION CRACKS DOWN ON FOREIGN WORKER VISA ABUSE — 8 MAJOR TECH COMPANIES TARGETED\n\nYesterday, the Trump administration announced a major escalation in its crackdown on alleged abuse of America’s foreign-worker visa system.\n\nEIGHT major technology companies have been suspended from the federal PERM labor certification process, which employers use to sponsor foreign workers for permanent residency.\n\nThe companies include:\n\n🔹 Microsoft\n🔹 Adobe\n🔹 Cognizant\n🔹 Infosys\n🔹 Tata Consultancy Services\n🔹 Wipro\n🔹 HCL Technologies\n🔹 Capgemini\n\nAnd here’s what makes this particularly interesting.\n\nVice President JD Vance highlighted Microsoft’s employment figures:\n\n🔥 Approximately 6,000 American workers laid off.\n🔥 Roughly 6,300 H-1B approvals.\n🔥 Nearly 3,000 green cards.\n\nThe administration is questioning whether American workers are being displaced while corporations continue sponsoring foreign labor.\n\nAND IT DOESN’T STOP WITH BIG TECH.\n\nNine major universities, including Harvard, Yale, Stanford, MIT, and Brown, are also facing investigations involving potential abuse of the separate J-1 exchange visitor program.\n\nThe DOJ is examining potential violations, with civil and criminal enforcement possible if wrongdoing is established.\n\nUnderstand the distinction: These are suspensions from a green-card certification process and investigations into alleged abuses — NOT a blanket cancellation of H-1B visas or proof that the companies committed fraud.\n\nBut the broader development is significant.\n\nFor years, critics have argued that America’s immigration and employment systems have allowed major corporations to prioritize cheaper foreign labor while American workers face layoffs and wage pressure.\n\nNow the federal government is putting some of the biggest names in technology under direct scrutiny.\n\nThe question is no longer simply whether the system needs reform.\n\nIt’s whether federal investigators can establish that corporations deliberately manipulated the system — and what consequences will follow.\n\n🇺🇸 AMERICAN WORKERS FIRST.\n\n🇺🇸🟨🇺🇸",
